{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "expand-ev-heat-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.50: the `expand-ev-heat` run computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE through `moves-onroad.esm`. Battery-electric passenger cars (21) and transit buses (42), Washtenaw, 2020, August weekday, hour 16 (heat index 83.16 degF), road types 2-5, running Total Energy. WHAT IT DISCRIMINATES: the EV running-energy temperature adjustment is zeroed for light duty (source type < 40) above a 67 degF heat index (adjust.rs) -- so it must be zeroed for 21 and NOT for 42. Every earlier EV run selects source type 21 alone, where `run_evTemperatureIsSuppressed` reading the run's FIRST source type and reading each source type agree; here they do not. The RunSpec also selects PM10 brake and tire wear; MOVES writes no rows for them (PM10 wear without its PM2.5 parent), so this run does not cover wear on several road types.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "expand-ev-heat"
    ]
  },
